    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0529" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW 1939/2635</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Central
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Riddleberger</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to Mr. Fletcher Warren, Executive Assistant to the
                        Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-22">May 22, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Warren</hi>: I return herewith the O.S.S.
                        report<anchor n="9" xml:id="d283-f1"/> on the most recent German peace
                    feeler in Switzerland. Under arrangements made at Moscow,<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d283-f2"/> the three powers are supposed to inform one another of
                    any peace feelers which they may receive. I have consequently drafted
                    communications to the British and Soviet Embassies advising them of this
                        matter.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d283-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Could you request O.S.S. to inform its representative in Switzerland of the
                    position of this government with respect to such peace feelers.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d283-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Riddleberger</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d283-f1" n="9" xml:id="d283-f1-content">
                <p>Dated May 16, <ref target="#pg510">p. 510</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d283-f2" n="10" xml:id="d283-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the Tripartite Conference of Foreign Ministers, October
                    18–November 1, 1943, see <ref target="frus1943v01#pg_513">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. 1, pp. 513</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d283-f3" n="11" xml:id="d283-f3-content">
                <p>See footnote 90, <ref target="#pg510">p. 510</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d283-f4" n="12" xml:id="d283-f4-content">
                <p>Marginal note in text, presumably in reply to this request, read as follows:
                    “This will be done when file is returned to me after <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-m</hi>[<hi rendition="#italic">émoire</hi>]’s are sent.” See footnote
                    90, <ref target="#pg510">p. 510</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
